## What was delivered

`src/ExtractionWorkflow/` — the deterministic coordination module's foundation:
the document-intelligence and extraction-only content-read ports plus
`ExtractionSourceLease`; the safe result shapes (`ExtractionVersion`,
`ExtractionBoxValue`, `ClassificationOutcome`, `FieldValidationOutcome`,
`MedicalEvidenceVersion`, `CurrencyDeclaration`); the untrusted provider results;
the closed field, error, and enum vocabularies; and `ExtractionPayloadBuilder`,
the single in-memory `T4RawInput` assembly path.

`src/DocumentIntelligence/` — `DeterministicDocumentIntelligenceProvider`, its
fail-closed options guard, and the Development/test-only registration extension.

Nothing in either project is a stub: no `NotImplementedException`, no empty
project, no unused public contract, and no unused project reference.

## The invariants that are types, not filters

- `ExtractionBoxValue` refuses `T4BoxCodes.SocialInsuranceNumber` at
  construction, in every spelling, and exposes no public constructor or factory
  returning an instance.
- `CorrectionField` declares no Box 12 member, and no member naming the
  server-derived tax year, the firm/case/participant/document/content-key scope,
  a CRA line, or a validation result.
- `ExtractionPayloadBuilder.Build` hands the assembled payload to a continuation
  and never returns it, so Box 12 exists only for the duration of one call and
  reaches no result shape, `ToString()`, error message, or serialization.

## Repository registrations — the authorized amendment

Four new project paths cannot exist without joining two closed registries, and
neither file was in T02's original list. `tasks.md` was amended narrowly to
record the ownership, exactly as spec 014 T01 did for the same defect.

`scripts/Assert-DotNet10Toolchain.ps1` — added exactly four paths to
`$approvedProjects`:

        src/DocumentIntelligence/DocumentIntelligence.csproj
        src/ExtractionWorkflow/ExtractionWorkflow.csproj
        tests/DocumentIntelligence.Tests/DocumentIntelligence.Tests.csproj
        tests/ExtractionWorkflow.Tests/ExtractionWorkflow.Tests.csproj

The closed registry is preserved and every existing SDK, target-framework,
solution-membership, xunit.v3, test-package, and framework-package check is
unweakened. Nothing was removed.

`tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/UpgradeBaselineContractTests.cs` — the exact
assertion "the modules added since the spec 013 baseline are exactly
`[ClientIntake]`" was **replaced**, not extended. Extending it would make every
future approved module break a historical .NET 10 baseline test that has nothing
to say about it — the closed-set trap this repository has now hit three times.
The replacement asserts, individually and openly:

- `ClientIntake`, `ExtractionWorkflow`, and `DocumentIntelligence` are each
  declared exactly once at their approved path, in the solution file and among
  the production project names;
- each is genuinely post-baseline, so this list cannot become a way to exempt a
  baseline assembly from the signature comparison;
- every baseline production project is still declared — an assertion that fails
  if one disappeared, never because one was added;
- no total or permanently closed set of solution projects is asserted.

Every baseline signature, friend-assembly, embedded-resource, migration-byte, and
test-floor comparison in that file is byte-for-byte unchanged, and no production
`TaxAI.Portal` code was touched.

## Project references

`src/ExtractionWorkflow/ExtractionWorkflow.csproj` declares exactly the three
references T02's own working code consumes:

        ../DocumentExtraction/DocumentExtraction.csproj
        ../TaxLogicEngine/TaxLogicEngine.csproj
        ../Tenancy/Tenancy.csproj

`CaseProcessing`, `CaseReview`, and `ClientIntake` are deliberately **not**
pre-added for later waves: a reference no code names is an unused reference.
`tasks.md` now gives T04 and T05 sequential ownership of this file so each adds
the reference it is first to consume. `BoundaryTests` enforces both halves — the
declared set, and that every declared reference appears in the compiled
assembly's reference list.

## Boundaries verified

- No OCR, LLM, document-intelligence, cloud, or HTTP-client package in any
  project in the repository. `DocumentIntelligence` declares exactly one package,
  `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions` 10.0.10, for its single
  registration extension.
- No repository-owned assembly reachable from either module names a
  `System.Net.*` assembly, no executable line names a network API, and the whole
  classify-and-extract flow completes without pulling in a networking assembly.
  The end-to-end run with outbound access actually blocked belongs to T07.
- No executable line in either module logs, caches, or writes a provider payload
  or a source byte.
- No CRA line-number literal, box→line table, box-code-keyed tax decision, rate,
  threshold, arithmetic operator on a tax value, `Math.Round`, `double`, `float`,
  or mapping-resource read. The `decimal` token appears only as confidence.
- No supported-year list, current-year concept, adjacent-year fallback, or
  four-digit tax-year literal in either module.
- No clock, environment, current-user, `HttpContext`, `Guid.NewGuid`, or
  randomness read: instants and actor references are parameters.
- Every public instance type is a sealed class, never a record, with a
  hand-written `ToString()` emitting counts, closed enum values, and presence
  flags only. Every identifier, taxpayer-text, and content-key property is
  `[JsonIgnore]`.
- A planted `123456789` reaches no result shape, `ToString()`, error message, or
  serialization; a nine-consecutive-digit sweep is the assertion.
- The only executable mention of the SIN box in either module is the invariant
  that refuses it, and it names the engine's own constant so the two cannot drift.
- Each new project is asserted exactly once at its approved path, never as part
  of a closed project set.

## Not in this task, and absent from the tree

No `IExtractionStore`, EF entity, or migration (T03). No ingest workflow,
`DocumentExtractionIngress`, medical validator, duplicate detector, or projection
(T04). No review workflow, correction, override, or acceptance path (T05). No
HTTP route, component, content-reader implementation, or composition-root wiring
(T06). No verification record (T07).

No production document-intelligence provider, no network egress, no
source-content preview, download, print, email, or export path, no retention or
purge path, and no deployment authorization. The spec 011 deployment refusal, the
spec 012 review route, the twelve spec 014 intake routes, the existing
migrations, and every existing public contract are untouched.
